\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, AUGUST 1, 2007\r\rMayor Bozajian called the meeting to order at 7:00 p.m. in Conference Room No. 2, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Bozajian, Mayor pro Tem Maurer, Councilmembers Groveman, Washburn, Wolfson.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles, Tamuri.\r\rCLOSED SESSION\r\rThe City Council recessed at 7:01 p.m. into closed session to confer with legal counsel regarding the following:\r\r1. Real property negotiations, pursuant to Government Code Section 54956.8.\rAgency Negotiator:�� Maureen Tamuri, Community Development Director.\rNegotiating parties:�� City of Calabasas and Currey-Riach / RCS Development.\rInstruction: Discussion regarding negotiations on lot located on southwest corner of Lost Hills and Calabasas Hills Roads. \rIdentity of property:��Assessors Parcel Number 2063-043-015.�\r2. \u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015Existing litigation, pursuant to Government Code Section 54956.9(a), Department of Fish & Game v. Shea Homes. \r\rThe City Council reconvened at 7:20 p.m. from closed session and Mayor Bozajian called the meeting to order at 7:30 p.m. in the City Council Chambers of City Hall, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Bozajian, Mayor pro Tem Maurer, Councilmembers Groveman, Washburn, Wolfson.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles, Peirce, Rubin, Tamuri, Yalda.\r\rThe Pledge of Allegiance was led by Ruth McBain.\r\rMichael G. Colantuono, City Attorney, stated that the Council did not take any action in closed session which required reporting. The City Council requested that the City Attorney prepare and post an explanatory brief regarding the lawsuit, Fish & Game v. Shea Homes on the City website.\r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r\r Councilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to approve the agenda. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS\r\r Mayor pro Tem Maurer announced an upcoming meeting regarding the proposed development at Lost Hills Road and Agoura Road. Mayor Bozajian spoke regarding upcoming events in the City. He spoke regarding the groundbreaking of the Las Virgenes Creek Project.\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT\r\r Dale Reicheneder, Calabasas, spoke regarding the General Plan Advisory Committee and expressed concern over absenteeism and potential future developments. Martin Atkinson-Barr, Calabasas, spoke regarding a recent article in �The Acorn� regarding the traffic signal at Old Topanga Canyon and Mulholland Highway and comments made by staff members of the City. Toby Keeler, Calabasas, spoke regarding the general plan update and expressed concern over the proceedings of the General Plan Advisory Committee.\r\rCONSENT ITEMS\r \r Approval of the minutes for the July 11, 2007 City Council meeting.\r\r Recommendation to adopt Resolution No. 2007-1083, authorizing the City Manager to file a Declaration of Interest by the California State Library at the Civic Center Site.\r\r Recommendation to award a contract to Advanced Construction and Restoration for sign and sign post installation services.\r\r Recommendation to amend the professional services agreement with Interior Space International (ISI) in the amount of $40,000 for additional services on the Civic Center project.\r\r Approval of a memorandum of understanding with Calabasas Village Mobile Estates for senior and disabled rental assistance program.\r\r Recommendation to send a letter of support for SB 990 (Kuehl), regarding the highest level of cleanup at the Santa Susana Field Laboratory.\r\r Authorization to execute two professional services agreements with Jonathan Kramer for specialty telecommunications consulting services in the total amount of $50,000 for two years.\r\r Amendment to the professional services agreement for as-needed inspection and testing services in the amount of $146,217 to Twinings Laboratory of Southern California.\r\r Recommendation to approve an appointment to the Agoura Hills/Calabasas Community Center Joint Powers Authority Board.\r\r Authorization to execute a professional services agreement with LDM Associates, Inc., to provide Community Development Block Grant (CDBG) administrative services for FY 2007-2008.\r\r Recommendation to approve City Streets for Major Maintenance per the City�s Pavement Management System and to authorize construction contracts and a professional service agreement for construction inspection.�\r\r Recommendation to award a construction contract for the Mulholland Highway Median Improvement project, Specification No. 07-08-03.\r\r Recommendation to rescind the construction contract to G. Coast Construction in the amount of $755,763 for the U.S. 101 Corridor Bike Lane Gap Closure at Mureau Road project and to award a construction contract to Barry General Engineering in the amount of $862,300 for the U.S. 101 Corridor Bike Lane Gap Closure at Mureau Road project.\r\r Recommendation from the School Partnership Task Force to approve an MOU with the Las Virgenes Unified School District (LVUSD) establishing guidelines for the distribution of interest accrued in the City/LVUSD school trust account.\r\rCouncilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Groveman, to approve Consent Items #1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rFollowing discussion, Councilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Maurer to approve Consent Items #5 and 14. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rFollowing discussion, Councilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Groveman to award the bid to the second lowest bidder in Item #13. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rPUBLIC HEARING\r \r Request for a Conditional Use Permit, Oak Tree Permit, and a Tentative Tract Map to construct a 86 unit multi-family residential development on 5 acres of a 21 acre site (16 acres will remain open space) located within the Commercial, Limited zoning district and a designated scenic corridor, at 4240 Las Virgenes Road (APN: 2069-011-005 and 2069-011-006).\r\rMayor Bozajian opened the public hearing.\r\rGeoffrey Starns, Senior Planner, and Elaine Camia, Assistant Engineer, presented the staff report.\r \rJeff Malone, John Matthews, Applicant, Standard Pacific Homes, Ronald Shmerling, Geolabs, presented background information on the proposed project. Gene Talmadge, Las Virgenes Municipal Water District, spoke in support of all of the findings in the resolution be adopted in order to address concerns raised by the LVMWD. Sergeant Brooks, Los Angeles County Sheriff�s Department, spoke in support of the proposed road widening for the project. Jeanette Mopey, Rachel Heller, Dale Reicheneder, representing Steeplechase Homeowners Association, Frank Joseph, Stonecreek Homeowners Association, Thom Slosson, Slosson & Associates, Margaret Maseda, representing Malibu Creek Homeowners Association, Lynne Tracey, Calabasas, Toby Keeler, Calabasas, Ellie Bracken, representing Malibu Canyon Villas, Denise Miller, Stonecreek, Donna Lane, Calabasas View Homeowners Association and Westside Coalition, Sherry Radis, Mira Monte, Melissa Olen, Calabasas, Norman Buehring, representing Saratoga Hills Homeowners Association, Patricia Threlkel, Stonecreek, Tami Louis, Stonecreek, Leon Koziewicz, Calabasas, Brian Louis, Stonecreek Homeowners Association, Nolan Burkholder, Calabasas, Mary Hubbard, representing Malibu Canyon Homeowners Association, Diane Stonefield, Stonecreek, Darlene Orlando, Bob Robbins, Calabasas, Karen Tiffany, Calabasas, Don Wallace, Cold Creek, spoke in opposition to the project as it is currently proposed. Alex Mogtaderi, William Whitman, Marlene Ahlquist, Kristin Pifko, did not speak, but presented speaker cards in opposition to the proposed project. Erik Pontoppidan, spoke in opposition to the tandem parking proposed in the project. \r\rThe City Council recessed at 10:00 p.m. and reconvened at 10:05 p.m.\r\rMayor Bozajian closed the public hearing.\r\rCouncilmember Groveman moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to adopt Resolution No. 2007-1097, adopting the Mitigated Negative Declaration and Mitigation Monitoring and Reporting Program (MMRP) and approving File Nos. CUP-003-013, OAK-003-017 and TT60488. MOTION CARRIED 3/2. Mayor Bozajian and Mayor pro Tem Maurer voted NO.\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS \r\r Report from Steve Harris and Debbie Bruschaber from the MRT regarding the Dry Canyon Creek restoration project and report from Alex Farassati regarding the upcoming Las Virgenes Creek restoration project.\r\rCouncilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson to table the item. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\r Check Register for the period of June 28, 2007 to July 19, 2007.\r\rThere was no action taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS\r\r There were no task force reports.\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT\r\r City Manager Coroalles indicated he had nothing to report.\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS\r\r Mayor pro Tem Maurer requested that an item regarding scenic corridor guidelines be agendized on a future agenda.\r\rADJOURN\r\r The City Council adjourned at 11:25 p.m. in memory of Gerald Mooney, father of Patty Coroalles.\r\r\r\r\r______________________________\rGwen Peirce, CMC\rAssistant City Clerk\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u00142\u0015\r08/01/07\r\r\u0013PAGE \u00144\u0015\r08/01/07\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u000